multichoice[30]{tags,text,exhibit,correct,w1,w2,w3,explanation,bloom,difficulty}:
  "objective:cisco:300-435:1.1|objective:cisco:300-635:1.1|topic:yang","Which YANG statement defines a reusable set of nodes that can be included in several places of a model?",,"grouping","typedef","identity","augment","A grouping holds nodes that other parts of the model include with uses. A typedef defines a reusable type, an identity defines a named abstract value, and augment adds nodes to another module's tree.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:1.2|objective:cisco:350-901:1.3|topic:restconf","Which RESTCONF root resource does a client use to invoke an RPC, such as a reload operation?",,"/restconf/operations","/restconf/data","/restconf/yang-library-version","/restconf/streams","RFC 8040 defines /restconf/operations for RPC and action invocation. /restconf/data is the datastore, and the other resources describe the YANG library and notification streams.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:1.5|objective:cisco:300-635:1.5|topic:yang|topic:rfc8340","In an RFC 8340 module tree, what does a question mark after a node name mean?",,"The node is optional","The node is a list","The node is read-only state","The node is a choice","In the tree notation, ? marks an optional node. An asterisk marks a list or leaf-list, ro marks state data, and a choice is shown in parentheses.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.1|topic:netmiko","When is send_command_timing the better Netmiko method than send_command?",,"When a command shows an interactive prompt or the prompt cannot be detected reliably","When the command output must be parsed with TextFSM","When the session needs more than one thread","When the device uses the default enable password","send_command_timing waits for the output to stop arriving instead of looking for the prompt, which suits prompts that change or confirmations. TextFSM parsing, threads and passwords are not what it is for.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.1|topic:netmiko","A Netmiko session to a cisco_ios device lands in user EXEC mode. Which call enters privileged EXEC mode?",,"conn.enable(), using the secret that was passed to ConnectHandler","conn.config_mode()","conn.exit_enable_mode()","conn.find_prompt()","enable() sends the enable command and the secret to enter privileged EXEC mode. config_mode enters configuration mode, exit_enable_mode leaves privileged mode, and find_prompt only reads the prompt.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.2|objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|objective:cisco:350-901:1.4|topic:ncclient|topic:netconf","Which ncclient call retrieves operational state data as well as configuration?",,"m.get()","m.get_config()","m.edit_config()","m.copy_config()","The NETCONF get operation returns configuration and state data, while get-config returns configuration from a datastore only. edit-config changes configuration, and copy-config copies a datastore.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.3|objective:cisco:350-901:1.3|topic:restconf|topic:python","A RESTCONF POST creates a list entry that already exists. Which status code and error-tag does the server return?",,"409 Conflict with error-tag data-exists","400 Bad Request with error-tag missing-element","404 Not Found with error-tag invalid-value","201 Created with an empty body","RFC 8040 maps a create request for existing data to 409 with the data-exists error-tag. PUT would replace the entry instead, and 201 is returned only when the resource was created.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.4|topic:ansible","Which parameter of cisco.ios.ios_config places the lines under the interface GigabitEthernet1 section?",,"parents","before","after","match","parents names the section that the lines belong to, here the interface command. before and after add commands around the change, and match controls how the existing configuration is compared.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.5|topic:day-0","A Day-0 script must leave a switch reachable for Day-1 automation over SSH. Which set of commands must it contain?",,"A local user with privilege 15, an RSA key, SSH version 2 and transport input ssh on the vty lines","Only the hostname and a banner","Only an SNMP community string","Only the NTP server address","SSH access needs a user, a key pair, SSH enabled and the vty lines allowing it. A hostname, banner, SNMP or NTP setting does not give the automation a way to log in.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.6|topic:netconf|topic:troubleshooting","A NETCONF edit-config returns an rpc-error with error-tag unknown-element. What does it mean?",,"The payload contains an element that is not defined in the YANG model, for example with a wrong name or namespace","The user does not have the privilege to edit the datastore","Another session holds the lock on the datastore","The device does not support the datastore","unknown-element reports an element that the server does not know, usually a typo or a wrong namespace. Privilege problems return access-denied, and a held lock returns lock-denied.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.7|topic:eem","Which EEM event statement runs an applet when a syslog message matches a pattern?",,"event syslog pattern","event cli pattern","event timer cron","event snmp oid","The event syslog detector matches messages by pattern. event cli matches typed commands, timer cron matches times, and the SNMP detector watches an object ID.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.1|topic:meraki|topic:day-0","How does a new Meraki access point learn its configuration when it is powered on for the first time?",,"It contacts the Meraki cloud, which identifies it by serial number and sends the configuration of the network it is claimed to","It downloads its configuration from a TFTP server named in DHCP option 66","It waits for an engineer to log in to its console","It reads a configuration file from a USB drive only","Meraki devices call the cloud on first boot, and the cloud pushes the settings of the network that holds the claimed serial. No TFTP server or console work is needed.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.2|topic:meraki|topic:python","Which parameter of a Meraki Dashboard API list call sets how many items each page returns?",,"perPage","limit","pageSize","count","Meraki list endpoints accept perPage together with startingAfter or endingBefore, and the Link header gives the next page. limit, pageSize and count are not the parameter names.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.2|topic:catalyst-center|topic:python","After a script has obtained a token from Catalyst Center, which header carries it on later requests?",,"X-Auth-Token","Authorization: Bearer","X-API-Key","Cookie: JSESSIONID","Catalyst Center returns a token from the auth endpoint, and requests present it in the X-Auth-Token header. SD-WAN Manager uses a session cookie instead, and the other names are not used.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|topic:jinja2","Which Jinja2 feature lets a value that is changed inside a loop be used after the loop?",,"A namespace object","The set statement inside the loop","The loop.index variable","A macro without arguments","A variable assigned with set inside a loop is local to the loop, while an attribute of a namespace object can be updated inside the loop and read afterwards. loop.index only counts iterations.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.4|topic:ansible|topic:meraki","Which parameter passes the dashboard API key to the cisco.meraki Ansible modules?",,"auth_key","api_token","dashboard_key","password","The cisco.meraki modules take the API key in auth_key, and it can also come from an environment variable. The other names are not parameters of these modules.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.5|topic:meraki|topic:security","A script must quarantine one client by applying a group policy that blocks access. Which Meraki API resource does it update?",,"The client policy of the network, with devicePolicy set to Group policy and a groupPolicyId","The network's L3 firewall rules, replacing the whole list","The SSID's splash page settings","The organization's admin account","Applying a group policy to one client is done through the network's client policy. Editing firewall rules affects everyone, and the other resources do not control a single client.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.6|topic:sdwan|topic:troubleshooting","GET calls to SD-WAN Manager work with a valid session cookie, but a POST to the template API returns 403. What is the most likely cause?",,"The X-XSRF-TOKEN header from /dataservice/client/token is missing","The JSESSIONID cookie has the wrong name","The request must be sent over HTTP instead of HTTPS","The /dataservice prefix is not allowed for POST","From release 19.2, changing requests must carry the token that is obtained from /dataservice/client/token, in addition to the session cookie. A missing token produces 403.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.6|topic:ise|topic:troubleshooting","An ERS GET to the secondary policy administration node on port 9060 works, but a POST to it returns 401. Why?",,"Only the primary policy administration node accepts create and update requests on port 9060","The ERS API does not support POST","The request needs the X-XSRF-TOKEN header","Port 9060 is read-only for all nodes","With the ERS API on port 9060, reads can go to several nodes, but changes must go to the primary administration node. The API gateway on port 443 relaxes this.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.1|topic:sdwan|topic:day-0","Which action loads the list of WAN Edge devices that are allowed to join the SD-WAN fabric from a Smart Account?",,"Syncing the Smart Account in SD-WAN Manager","Typing the serial numbers into each edge's console","Setting a DHCP option on the branch router","Uploading the list to the SD-WAN Validator's flash","SD-WAN Manager can synchronize the authorized WAN Edge list from the Smart Account or accept an uploaded list, and the controllers then admit only those devices. Console or DHCP settings do not authorize an edge.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.1|topic:catalyst-center|topic:validation","A template deployment in Catalyst Center returns a taskId. How does a script learn whether the deployment finished?",,"Poll the task endpoint with that taskId until the task has an end time or reports an error","Wait for the response header to contain Done","Call the template API again with the same body","Read the device syslog","Catalyst Center work is asynchronous, and the task resource reports progress, completion and errors. Re-sending the request would deploy again.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.2|objective:cisco:350-901:2.4|topic:cml|topic:simulation","What is the difference between stopping and wiping a node in Cisco Modeling Labs?",,"Stopping keeps the node's configuration and disk, while wiping returns it to its initial state","Stopping deletes the node, while wiping only pauses it","Both actions delete the whole lab","Wiping keeps the configuration, while stopping erases it","Stopping a node powers it off but keeps its disk, so the configuration survives. Wiping removes that state, so the node boots as new.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.3|topic:sdwan|topic:software-management","After a new software version has been activated on a WAN Edge in SD-WAN Manager, which action makes it the version that the device keeps after a reboot?",,"Set it as the default version","Upload the image again","Detach the device template","Delete the previous image","Activation boots the new version, and setting it as the default confirms it for later reboots. Uploading again, detaching a template or deleting an image do not do that.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.4|topic:thousandeyes","Which ThousandEyes test type measures loss, latency and the network path between an agent and a target server?",,"An agent-to-server test","A page load test","A DNS server test","A voice (RTP) stream test","An agent-to-server test measures network performance and shows the path to a target. Page loads, DNS tests and voice streams test other behavior.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.6|objective:cisco:350-901:3.2|topic:catalyst-center|topic:webhooks","In the Catalyst Center API that creates a REST (webhook) event subscription, which value does connectorType take?",,"REST","SYSLOG","SNMP","EMAIL","A webhook subscription uses the REST connector, and the other connectors have their own subscription APIs. The notification is then posted to the URL of the endpoint.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.1|topic:ai|topic:catalyst-center","Why does an AI analytics platform need a learning period before it flags anomalies for a site?",,"It first learns what is normal for that site and time of day, and then reports deviations from that baseline","It must wait for the vendor to approve each alert","It cannot read telemetry until the period ends","It needs the period to download new device software","Anomaly detection compares current behavior with a learned baseline, so the system needs data from the site first. Alerts do not need vendor approval.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.2|objective:cisco:350-901:4.1|objective:cisco:300-635:5.1|topic:ai|topic:code-validation","An AI assistant writes requests.get(url, verify=False) in a script for production. What is the proper response?",,"Replace it with verification against the CA bundle that signed the controller certificate","Keep it, because the assistant is usually right","Keep it and add a comment","Remove the call and use HTTP instead","Disabling verification removes protection against man-in-the-middle attacks. The fix is to trust the right CA, and HTTP is worse.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.3|objective:cisco:350-901:4.2|objective:cisco:300-635:5.2|topic:ai|topic:ai-security","A coding assistant indexes a repository that contains a .env file with API keys. What is the main risk, and what is the control?",,"The keys can reach the assistant's provider, so exclude secret files from indexing and keep secrets in a vault","The assistant will run slower, so add more memory","The assistant will rewrite the keys, so make the file read-only","The repository will exceed its size limit, so compress it","Anything the assistant can read may leave the organization. Secrets should be excluded from its context and kept in a vault, not in files in the repository.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.4|objective:cisco:350-901:4.3|objective:cisco:300-635:5.3|topic:mcp","Which element of an MCP server is a reusable template with parameters that a client can offer to the user?",,"A prompt","A tool","A resource","A transport","MCP servers can expose tools, resources and prompts. A prompt is a parameterized instruction template, a tool is an action, and a resource is read-only context.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.2|objective:cisco:350-901:4.1|objective:cisco:300-635:5.1|topic:ai|topic:llm","Which prompt practice best reduces invented API endpoints in generated controller scripts?",,"Provide the OpenAPI specification or the documentation of the endpoints in the prompt","Ask for a script without comments","Ask the model to try several answers and pick the longest","Remove the controller name from the prompt","Grounding the model in the real API definition limits invention. Comments, length and removing the product name do not.",3,2

multiselect[30]{tags,text,exhibit,c1,c2,c3,w1,w2,w3,explanation,bloom,difficulty}:
  "objective:cisco:300-435:1.3|objective:cisco:350-901:2.7|objective:cisco:300-635:1.5|topic:yang|topic:json","Which two rules apply when a JSON payload is built from a YANG model? (Choose two.)",,"The top-level member is qualified with the module name, as in ietf-interfaces:interfaces","A list is written as an array of objects",,"A list is written as a single object","Boolean values are written as strings","The module name is omitted from every member","RFC 7951 qualifies a top-level node with its module name and encodes lists as arrays. Lists are not single objects, booleans are JSON booleans, and the module name is not dropped.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:1.4|objective:cisco:300-635:1.5|topic:yang|topic:xml","Which two rules apply when an XML payload is built from a YANG model? (Choose two.)",,"The element carries the module's namespace URI","The key of a list entry is written as a child element",,"The module name is used as the namespace","The key of a list entry is written as an XML attribute","The namespace is left out when the element is a leaf","In XML encoding the namespace URI identifies the module, and list keys are child elements. The module name is not a namespace, and attributes are used for protocol attributes, not keys.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:1.2|objective:cisco:300-635:1.4|topic:netconf","Which two features does NETCONF offer that RESTCONF does not? (Choose two.)",,"Locking a datastore against changes from other sessions","Applying several changes together with the candidate datastore and commit when the device supports it",,"Encoding data as JSON","Addressing data with URIs","Using HTTP status codes for errors","Locks and candidate commits belong to NETCONF. JSON encoding, URIs and HTTP status codes are RESTCONF characteristics, and each RESTCONF request is applied on its own.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.1|topic:netmiko","Which two Netmiko methods change the configuration of a device? (Choose two.)",,"send_config_set()","send_config_from_file()",,"send_command()","find_prompt()","disconnect()","send_config_set and send_config_from_file enter configuration mode and send configuration commands. send_command runs a command in the current mode, and the others only read the prompt or close the session.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.1|topic:netmiko","Which two practices speed up a Netmiko script that configures many devices? (Choose two.)",,"Run the per-device work in parallel with a thread pool","Reuse one session for several commands instead of reconnecting for each command",,"Open a new session for every command","Add time.sleep(10) after every command","Run the devices one after another","The work waits mostly on the network, so threads help, and reconnecting costs time. Extra sleeps and serial runs make the script slower.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.2|objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|objective:cisco:350-901:1.4|topic:ncclient|topic:netconf","Which two capabilities must the server advertise before an ncclient script uses the candidate datastore with a confirmed commit? (Choose two.)",,"urn:ietf:params:netconf:capability:candidate:1.0","urn:ietf:params:netconf:capability:confirmed-commit:1.1",,"urn:ietf:params:netconf:capability:xpath:1.0","urn:ietf:params:netconf:capability:writable-running:1.0","urn:ietf:params:netconf:capability:url:1.0","The candidate capability provides the datastore, and confirmed-commit adds the timed commit. The others describe XPath filters, writing to running and URL sources.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.3|objective:cisco:350-901:1.3|objective:cisco:350-901:1.4|topic:restconf|topic:python","Which two headers should a RESTCONF request that sends and receives JSON carry? (Choose two.)",,"Content-Type: application/yang-data+json","Accept: application/yang-data+json",,"Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded","Accept: text/html","X-Auth-Token: <token>","RESTCONF uses the yang-data media types for the body and the reply. Form encoding, HTML and a controller token header are not used by a device's RESTCONF server.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.4|topic:ansible","Which two inventory variables let Ansible manage an IOS XE device with the cisco.ios modules over SSH? (Choose two.)",,"ansible_connection: ansible.netcommon.network_cli","ansible_network_os: cisco.ios.ios",,"ansible_connection: local","ansible_network_os: cisco.nxos.nxos","ansible_python_interpreter: /usr/bin/python3 on the device","The cisco.ios modules use the network_cli connection and the cisco.ios.ios network OS. A local connection runs on the control node, nxos is another platform, and the device's Python is not used.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.5|topic:ztp|topic:day-0","Which two things happen when a switch with no configuration receives DHCP option 67 that names a Python script for ZTP? (Choose two.)",,"The switch downloads the script","The script runs in Guest Shell with access to the cli module",,"The script runs on the DHCP server","The switch contacts Catalyst Center to download its configuration","The script must be signed by Cisco","IOS XE ZTP fetches the script named in option 67 and runs it in Guest Shell, where it can use the cli module. It does not run on the server or need Catalyst Center.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.6|topic:restconf|topic:troubleshooting","Which two causes produce a 400 response with error-tag invalid-value in RESTCONF? (Choose two.)",,"A number outside the range that the YANG model allows","A string that does not match the pattern of the leaf",,"A missing Accept header","An unknown URI path","Credentials that are not valid","Values that break a type restriction produce invalid-value. A missing header, an unknown path and bad credentials produce other codes, such as 406, 404 and 401.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.7|topic:eem","Which two are valid EEM applet actions? (Choose two.)",,"action 1.0 cli command \"show version\"","action 2.0 syslog msg \"done\"",,"action 1.0 netconf get-config","action 2.0 restconf get","action 3.0 terraform apply","EEM applets can run CLI commands and generate syslog messages, among other actions. There are no NETCONF, RESTCONF or Terraform actions.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.1|topic:meraki|topic:day-0","Which two ways bring a Meraki switch under dashboard management? (Choose two.)",,"Claim it by serial number","Claim it with the order number of the purchase",,"Install a Meraki agent on it","Import its running configuration","Point it to a TFTP server","Meraki devices are claimed into an organization by serial number or by order number, and they then appear in the inventory. There is no agent or configuration import.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.1|topic:catalyst-center|topic:pnp","Which two methods can lead a PnP-capable switch to Catalyst Center? (Choose two.)",,"DHCP option 43 with the controller address","DNS resolution of pnpserver in the local domain",,"SNMP trap from the controller","A static route to the cloud","Console input only","A PnP agent finds the controller from DHCP option 43 or from DNS, and cloud redirection is a third method. SNMP traps and static routes do not provide the controller address.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.2|topic:sdwan|topic:python","Which two steps does a script take to authenticate to SD-WAN Manager release 19.2 or later? (Choose two.)",,"POST the credentials to /j_security_check and keep the JSESSIONID cookie","GET /dataservice/client/token and send the result in X-XSRF-TOKEN",,"POST to /dna/system/api/v1/auth/token","Send an X-Auth-Token header","Send the password in every query string","SD-WAN Manager uses a session cookie and, from 19.2, a token for requests. The Catalyst Center token endpoint and header are not used, and passwords do not belong in query strings.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|topic:jinja2","Which two Jinja2 expressions help to render a list of VLAN names as one comma-separated line? (Choose two.)",,"map(attribute='name')","join(', ')",,"upper","first","length","map selects the attribute from every item, and join builds one string. upper changes case, first returns one item and length counts.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.4|topic:ansible|topic:meraki","Which two parameters identify the network that a cisco.meraki module works on? (Choose two.)",,"net_name","net_id",,"network_serial","net_vlan","net_policy","The modules accept the network by name or by ID. The other names are not parameters of these modules.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.5|topic:ise|topic:security","Which two statements about the REST APIs of Cisco ISE are correct? (Choose two.)",,"ERS is served on port 9060 and uses basic authentication","The OpenAPI is served on port 443 and returns JSON",,"ERS uses WebSocket and mutual TLS","The OpenAPI is served on port 9060","pxGrid is a configuration API on port 9060","ERS uses basic authentication on port 9060, and the OpenAPI uses port 443. WebSocket with mutual TLS describes pxGrid, which has its own port.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.5|topic:sdwan|topic:segmentation","Which two statements about segmentation in Cisco SD-WAN are correct? (Choose two.)",,"Service VPNs isolate traffic of different groups from one another","VPN 0 carries the transport and VPN 512 is for management",,"VPN 0 is a service VPN for users","All VPNs share one routing table","Segmentation needs a separate controller for each VPN","SD-WAN segments traffic with VPNs, similar to VRFs, and VPN 0 is the transport while VPN 512 is for management. Service VPNs have their own routing tables.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.6|objective:cisco:350-901:1.6|topic:meraki|topic:troubleshooting","Which two items tell a client how to react to a Meraki 429 response? (Choose two.)",,"The Retry-After header","An errors list in the response body that states that the rate limit was exceeded",,"The X-Auth-Token header","A Location header with a new URL","The Link header with the next page","A 429 means too many requests, and Retry-After says how many seconds to wait. The body explains the error. Tokens, locations and pagination links are unrelated.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.6|topic:catalyst-center|topic:troubleshooting","A Catalyst Center call returns 403 for one user while the same call works for another user. Which two checks help? (Choose two.)",,"The role and permissions of the user","Whether the token belongs to the intended user and has not expired",,"The version of the requests library","The TCP window size","Whether HTTP/2 is enabled","A 403 means the caller is known but not allowed, so the role and the identity of the token matter. Library versions and network settings do not cause it.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.1|objective:cisco:350-901:3.4|objective:cisco:300-635:4.2|topic:pyats|topic:validation","Which two practices make pyATS pre-change and post-change validation reliable? (Choose two.)",,"Learn the same features on the same devices before and after the change","Compare the two snapshots with a diff and review the result",,"Take only a post-change snapshot","Learn different features before and after","Skip the diff when the pipeline is green","A comparison is only meaningful when both snapshots describe the same things, and the diff must be reviewed. A single snapshot or different features cannot show a change.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.3|topic:catalyst-center|topic:swim","Which two tasks belong to software image management in Catalyst Center? (Choose two.)",,"Distributing an image to a device","Activating an image on a device",,"Rendering a Jinja2 template","Creating a site hierarchy","Subscribing to a webhook","SWIM imports, distributes and activates images. Templates, sites and webhooks are other features.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.4|topic:meraki|topic:monitoring","Which two approaches detect that a Meraki device went offline? (Choose two.)",,"Query the device statuses of the organization","Receive a webhook alert from the dashboard",,"Wait for the device to send an SNMP trap to the API gateway","Read the device's local syslog from the API","Poll the Catalyst Center health score","The dashboard offers status queries and alert webhooks. The other options are not part of the Meraki API.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.5|objective:cisco:350-901:3.1|objective:cisco:300-635:4.3|topic:telemetry|topic:mdt","Which two update triggers can a model-driven telemetry subscription use? (Choose two.)",,"Periodic updates at a set interval","On-change updates when a value changes",,"Updates only when the collector polls","Updates only at reload","Updates only when an SNMP trap arrives","Subscriptions push data periodically or when the value changes. Polling by the collector, reload and traps are not subscription triggers.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.6|objective:cisco:350-901:3.2|topic:webhooks|topic:security","Which two practices make a webhook receiver safer? (Choose two.)",,"Verify the shared secret or signature that the sender includes","Accept requests only over HTTPS",,"Accept requests from any sender without checks","Put the shared secret in the URL path of a public page","Disable logging of received events","A receiver should check that an event comes from the expected sender and should use HTTPS. Open endpoints, exposed secrets and missing logs weaken it.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.1|topic:ai|topic:catalyst-center","Which two statements about AI-based endpoint profiling are correct? (Choose two.)",,"Machine learning can group unknown endpoints by their behavior","Suggested profiles can feed policy decisions after an administrator reviews them",,"It removes the need for any administrator review","It works without any data from the network","It assigns a profile that cannot be changed","Profiling uses telemetry to cluster endpoints, and administrators review the suggestions before policy relies on them. It needs data and remains under administrator control.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.2|objective:cisco:350-901:4.1|objective:cisco:300-635:5.1|topic:ai|topic:code-validation","Which two checks should be applied to AI-generated automation code before it runs on production devices? (Choose two.)",,"Review it against the documentation of the APIs it calls","Run it in a lab or simulation with tests",,"Run it on production once to see what happens","Ask the assistant whether the code is correct","Accept it when it passes a syntax check","Generated code can use calls that do not exist, so it needs review and testing in a safe place. The assistant's own opinion and a syntax check do not prove behavior.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.3|objective:cisco:350-901:4.2|objective:cisco:300-635:5.2|topic:ai|topic:ai-security","Which two controls limit the damage of a prompt injection against a network agent? (Choose two.)",,"Give the agent only the permissions that its tasks need","Require human approval before changes are applied",,"Let the agent follow instructions found in any log it reads","Give the agent a shared administrator account","Remove all logging of agent actions","An injected instruction can only do what the agent is allowed to do, and approval stops unwanted changes. Obeying log text, broad accounts and missing logs increase the damage.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.4|objective:cisco:350-901:4.3|objective:cisco:300-635:5.3|topic:mcp","Which two statements about an MCP server that is started by a desktop client are correct? (Choose two.)",,"It commonly runs as a local process and talks to the client over standard input and output","The client configuration names the command and arguments that start it",,"It must listen on a public port","It needs the model to run it as code","It can only expose resources, not tools","A locally started server uses the stdio transport, and the client configuration says how to start it. It does not need a public port, and it can expose tools, resources and prompts.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.2|objective:cisco:350-901:4.5|objective:cisco:300-635:5.1|topic:ai|topic:validation","Which two actions help to measure how accurate an assistant is for a team's own tasks? (Choose two.)",,"Compare its answers with a set of questions that have known correct answers","Track how often its suggestions pass review and tests",,"Ask the assistant to rate its own confidence","Count how many suggestions it makes per day","Judge the answers by how detailed they sound","Accuracy is measured against known answers and against real outcomes. Self-rated confidence, volume and style do not measure correctness.",3,2

match[30]{tags,text,exhibit,p1,r1,p2,r2,p3,r3,p4,r4,p5,r5,explanation,bloom,difficulty}:
  "objective:cisco:300-435:1.5|objective:cisco:300-635:1.5|topic:yang|topic:rfc8340","Match each RFC 8340 tree symbol to its meaning.",,"rw","Configuration data that can be written","ro","State data that cannot be changed by a client","*","A list or leaf-list","[name]","The key of a list","(choice)","A choice with mutually exclusive cases","The tree notation shows whether data is configuration or state, whether it repeats, and how lists are keyed.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-435:1.2|objective:cisco:350-901:1.3|topic:restconf","Match each HTTP method to its RESTCONF operation.",,"GET","Reads a resource","POST","Creates a child resource or invokes an RPC","PUT","Creates or replaces a resource","PATCH","Merges changes into a resource","DELETE","Removes a resource","RESTCONF maps its operations onto HTTP methods. POST creates, PUT replaces, and PATCH merges.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:1.1|objective:cisco:300-635:1.1|topic:yang","Match each YANG statement to its purpose.",,"typedef","Defines a reusable data type","identity","Defines a named abstract value that other modules can derive from","choice","Allows exactly one of several alternative cases","must","Adds a constraint that is checked with an XPath expression","augment","Adds nodes to the tree of another module","Each statement shapes a model differently: types, identities, alternatives, constraints and extensions of other modules.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.1|topic:netmiko","Match each Netmiko call to what it does.",,"find_prompt()","Returns the current device prompt","enable()","Enters privileged EXEC mode","send_config_set()","Sends configuration commands in configuration mode","save_config()","Saves the running configuration to startup","disconnect()","Closes the session","The calls cover the life of a session: finding the prompt, changing modes, configuring, saving and closing.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.2|objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|topic:netconf","Match each NETCONF datastore to its description.",,"running","The configuration that is active on the device","candidate","A scratch configuration that is applied with a commit","startup","The configuration that is loaded at boot","operational","State data returned by the get operation","writable-running","A capability that allows edits directly in running","The datastores differ in whether they are active, staged or loaded at boot. Operational state is returned by get.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.3|topic:restconf","Match each RESTCONF error-tag to its meaning.",,"data-exists","A create request targets data that already exists","data-missing","The requested data does not exist","invalid-value","A value is not valid for its type or restrictions","access-denied","The user is not allowed to do the operation","in-use","The resource is locked or otherwise in use","Error-tags give the reason for a failure, and the HTTP status code groups them.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.4|topic:ansible","Match each cisco.ios module to its purpose.",,"ios_config","Sends configuration lines and sections","ios_command","Runs commands and returns their output","ios_facts","Collects information about the device","ios_vlans","Manages VLANs with a resource module","ios_interfaces","Manages interface attributes with a resource module","The cisco.ios collection has general modules and resource modules that manage one feature.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.5|topic:day-0","Match each DHCP option to its use in device provisioning.",,"Option 43","Vendor-specific information, such as the PnP controller string","Option 66","TFTP server name","Option 67","Boot file name, such as a ZTP script","Option 150","List of TFTP server addresses","Option 15","DNS domain name that is used to find pnpserver","The options carry the server, the file and the controller information that a device needs at first boot.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.6|objective:cisco:350-901:1.3|topic:troubleshooting|topic:restconf","Match each RESTCONF response to the request problem it most likely shows.",,"404 for interface=GigabitEthernet1/0/1","The slashes of the key are not percent-encoded","415 Unsupported Media Type","The Content-Type header is not a yang-data type","401 Unauthorized","Credentials are missing or not valid","400 with invalid-value","A value breaks a restriction of the model","409 with data-exists","The create request targets data that exists","Each response points to a different request error: encoding, headers, authentication, value or existing data.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.7|topic:guest-shell","Match each function of the IOS XE Guest Shell cli module to its behavior.",,"cli()","Runs a command and returns the output as a string","clip()","Runs a command and prints the output","configure()","Applies configuration commands","configurep()","Applies configuration commands and prints the result","from cli import ...","Imports the functions that the on-box scripts use","The module offers returning and printing forms of the same operations for show commands and configuration.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.3|topic:restconf","Match each RESTCONF query parameter to its effect.",,"content","Selects configuration, state or both","depth","Limits how many levels of the tree are returned","fields","Selects specific nodes of the resource","with-defaults","Controls how default values are reported","insert","Sets the position of a new entry in a user-ordered list","The query parameters shape the data that is returned or how new data is placed.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.1|topic:meraki","Match each Meraki object to its role.",,"Organization","Top-level account that holds networks and administrators","Network","Group of devices that share configuration","Device","A claimed access point, switch or appliance","Configuration template","Settings that bound networks inherit","SSID","A wireless network name with its own settings","The hierarchy goes from the organization to its networks and devices, and templates and SSIDs shape their settings.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.1|topic:catalyst-center|topic:pnp","Match each PnP device state in Catalyst Center to its meaning.",,"Unclaimed","The device contacted the controller and waits to be claimed","Planned","The device is added and assigned in advance","Onboarding","The device is being provisioned","Provisioned","Onboarding finished","Error","Onboarding failed","The states follow a device from discovery to a finished or failed onboarding.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.2|topic:sdwan|topic:python","Match each SD-WAN Manager API resource to its use.",,"/j_security_check","Logs in and returns the session cookie","/dataservice/client/token","Returns the token for the X-XSRF-TOKEN header","/dataservice/device","Lists the devices of the fabric","/dataservice/template/device","Lists device templates","/dataservice/device/action/status","Reports the progress of an action","Every call goes under /dataservice except the login. The resources cover session setup, inventory, templates and action status.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.2|objective:cisco:350-901:1.6|topic:meraki|topic:python","Match each Meraki Python library option to its effect.",,"total_pages='all'","Follows the pagination links and returns every page","wait_on_rate_limit","Waits and retries when the API answers 429","maximum_retries","Limits how many times a call is retried","suppress_logging","Turns off the library's log output","output_log","Writes a log file of the calls","The options control pagination, rate limit handling, retries and logging of the dashboard library.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|topic:jinja2","Match each Jinja2 loop variable to its value.",,"loop.index","The current iteration, starting at 1","loop.index0","The current iteration, starting at 0","loop.first","True in the first iteration","loop.last","True in the last iteration","loop.length","The number of items in the sequence","The loop object helps to format output, for example to omit a comma after the last item.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.4|topic:ansible|topic:meraki","Match each cisco.meraki module to what it manages.",,"meraki_organization","Organizations","meraki_network","Networks","meraki_ssid","Wireless SSIDs","meraki_vlan","VLANs of an appliance or switch network","meraki_admin","Dashboard administrators","The module names tell which Meraki object they manage.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.5|topic:ise|topic:security","Match each Cisco ISE security term to its meaning.",,"SGT","Security group tag that marks a group of users or devices","SGACL","Access list that applies between security groups","ANC policy","Adaptive network control action, such as quarantine, applied to an endpoint","Endpoint identity group","Group that an endpoint is a member of","pxGrid","Platform for sharing context and sessions with other security products","The terms cover segmentation by tags, endpoint response and the sharing of context.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.6|objective:cisco:350-901:1.6|topic:troubleshooting|topic:rest-api","Match each HTTP status of a controller API to its usual cause.",,"401","Missing or expired credentials or token","403","Authenticated user without permission","404","Wrong path or an object that the key cannot see","429","Rate limit exceeded","502 or 503","The service behind the gateway is unavailable","The status codes separate authentication, authorization, addressing, rate limiting and service problems.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.5|topic:sdwan|topic:segmentation","Match each Cisco SD-WAN term to its meaning.",,"VPN 0","The transport VPN","VPN 512","The management VPN","Service VPN","A VPN that carries user traffic of one segment","OMP","Protocol that carries routes and policy between edges and controllers","TLOC","Transport locator that identifies a WAN attachment point","The terms describe the transport, management and service segments and the control protocol of the fabric.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.1|topic:meraki|topic:validation","Match each Meraki live tool to what it checks.",,"ping","Reachability and latency from a device to a target","cableTest","The state of a switch port cable","throughputTest","Throughput of an appliance's connection","wakeOnLan","Wakes a client from the network","macTable","The MAC addresses that a switch has learned","The live tools run on the device itself and return results that a script can read after a change.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.2|objective:cisco:350-901:2.4|topic:cml|topic:simulation","Match each Cisco Modeling Labs element to its meaning.",,"Node definition","Describes the type and resources of a kind of node","External connector","Connects a lab to an outside network","Unmanaged switch","Simple switch that connects lab nodes","Topology file","YAML description of a lab","Lab","A set of nodes and links that run together","A lab is built from nodes of defined types, connectors and links, and the topology file describes it.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.3|topic:catalyst-center|topic:swim","Match each Catalyst Center SWIM term to its meaning.",,"Import","Adds an image to the repository","Distribute","Copies an image to a device","Activate","Boots the device with the image","Golden image","The image that is preferred for a device family and role","Image compliance","Comparison of the running image with the golden image","The terms describe the stages of an upgrade and the standard that devices are compared with.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.4|topic:thousandeyes","Match each ThousandEyes term to its meaning.",,"Enterprise agent","A vantage point installed in your own network","Cloud agent","A vantage point that ThousandEyes operates","Test","A scheduled measurement from agents to a target","Alert rule","Conditions that raise an alert about a test result","BGP monitor","A source of BGP routing data about prefixes","The terms cover where measurements start, what is measured and how problems are reported.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.5|objective:cisco:350-901:3.1|topic:telemetry|topic:mdt","Match each IOS XE telemetry configuration keyword to its role.",,"telemetry ietf subscription","Creates a configured subscription","filter xpath","Selects the data to stream","stream yang-push","Chooses the YANG-push stream","update-policy","Sets periodic or on-change updates","receiver ip address","Names the destination, port and protocol","These keywords build a configured subscription: its name, data, source, schedule and destination.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.6|objective:cisco:350-901:3.2|topic:webhooks","Match each webhook term to its meaning.",,"Payload","The data that the event sends","Subscription","The link between an event type and a destination","Endpoint","The URL that receives the event","Shared secret","A value that the receiver uses to verify the sender","Retry","A new delivery attempt after a failure","A webhook sends an event as an HTTP request to an endpoint, and secrets and retries make delivery safe and reliable.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.1|topic:ai|topic:analytics","Match each analytics term to its meaning.",,"Baseline","What is normal for a metric at a site","Anomaly","A value that deviates from the baseline","Clustering","Grouping similar items without labels","Correlation","Linking events that are likely related","False positive","An alert for something that is not a problem","The terms describe how analytics decides what is unusual, groups items and reports results.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.2|objective:cisco:350-901:4.1|topic:ai|topic:code-validation","Match each AI-assisted coding term to its meaning.",,"Hallucination","The model states invented details with confidence","Slopsquatting","Attackers register package names that models tend to invent","Prompt","The instruction and context that is given to the model","Context window","How much text the model can consider at once","Temperature","Setting that controls randomness of the output","The terms describe typical risks and settings of code assistants.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.3|objective:cisco:350-901:4.2|objective:cisco:300-635:5.2|topic:ai|topic:ai-security","Match each risk of an AI agent to its control.",,"Tool poisoning","Review tool descriptions and use vetted servers","Prompt injection","Treat data that the agent reads as untrusted","Excessive agency","Least privilege and approval for writes","Secret leakage","Redact secrets before they reach the model","Hallucinated command","Validate against documentation and test in a lab","Each risk has a specific control, from vetted tools to validation before a command runs.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.4|objective:cisco:350-901:4.3|objective:cisco:300-635:5.3|topic:mcp","Match each FastMCP element to its purpose.",,"@mcp.tool()","Exposes a function as an action that the model can call","@mcp.resource()","Exposes read-only data at a URI","@mcp.prompt()","Exposes a reusable prompt template","mcp.run()","Starts the server","Type hints","Define the input schema of a tool","The decorators map to the three kinds of MCP element, and run starts the server.",1,2

order[30]{tags,text,exhibit,s1,s2,s3,s4,s5,s6,explanation,bloom,difficulty}:
  "objective:cisco:300-435:1.3|objective:cisco:350-901:2.7|objective:cisco:300-635:1.5|topic:yang|topic:json","Place the steps of building a JSON payload from a YANG model in the correct order.",,"Find the module and the node to change","Print the tree to see the node types and keys","Write the module-qualified top-level member","Add the list as an array with its key leaves","Check the values against the types","Send the payload","The model is read before the payload is written, the values are checked, and the request is sent last.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:1.2|objective:cisco:350-901:1.3|topic:restconf","Place the steps of creating a list entry with RESTCONF in the correct order.",,"Build the URI of the parent resource","Build the JSON body with the new entry","Send a POST with the yang-data+json headers","Read the 201 Created response","Read the entry back with a GET",,"The URI and body are prepared, the POST creates the entry, and a GET confirms it.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:1.4|objective:cisco:300-635:1.5|topic:yang|topic:xml","Place the steps of producing an XML payload with a YANG tool in the correct order.",,"Load the YANG modules and their imports","Select the node that should be configured","Generate the XML skeleton for the node","Fill in the keys and values","Validate the XML against the model","Send it with edit-config","The tool needs the modules, the target node and its skeleton. The values are filled in and validated before the message is sent.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.1|topic:netmiko","Place the steps of a Netmiko script that changes and saves a configuration in the correct order.",,"Create the connection with ConnectHandler","Enter privileged mode if needed","Send the configuration with send_config_set","Check the result with a show command","Save with save_config","Disconnect","A session is opened, the change is made and verified, and the configuration is saved before the session closes.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.2|objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|objective:cisco:350-901:1.4|topic:ncclient|topic:netconf","Place the steps of a candidate datastore change with ncclient in the correct order.",,"Lock the candidate datastore","Send edit_config to the candidate","Validate the candidate","Commit","Unlock the datastore",,"A lock prevents other changes while the candidate is edited, validated and committed, and the lock is released afterwards.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.3|objective:cisco:350-901:1.3|objective:cisco:350-901:1.4|topic:restconf|topic:python","Place the steps of changing one leaf with RESTCONF and Python in the correct order.",,"Read the current value with GET","Build the PATCH body","Send the PATCH","Check the status code","Read the value again to verify",,"The current value is recorded before the change, the PATCH is sent and its status is checked, and a read confirms the result.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.4|topic:ansible","Place the steps of a safe rollout of a cisco.ios playbook in the correct order.",,"Run ansible-playbook with --syntax-check","Run it with --check and --diff","Review the proposed changes","Run it normally","Run it again and confirm that nothing changes",,"Syntax and a dry run come first, the changes are reviewed, and a second run proves idempotence.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.5|topic:ztp|topic:day-0","Place the events of IOS XE ZTP on a switch without a startup configuration in the correct order.",,"The switch boots and starts ZTP","It sends a DHCP request","The server answers with an address and the script name in option 67","The switch downloads the script","The script runs in Guest Shell","The switch is reachable for Day-1 automation","ZTP uses DHCP to find the script, which then runs in Guest Shell and configures the device.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.6|topic:restconf|topic:troubleshooting","Place the troubleshooting steps for a RESTCONF request that returns 401 in the correct order.",,"Read the status code and the error body","Check that RESTCONF and the HTTPS server are enabled","Check the user's privilege level","Repeat the request with curl and the same credentials","Fix the credentials or the role and retry",,"The error points to authentication, so the service, the user and a manual test narrow down the cause before the fix.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.7|topic:guest-shell","Place the steps of enabling Guest Shell on IOS XE in the correct order.",,"Enable the application hosting framework with iox","Configure the app-hosting appid guestshell with a virtual interface","Enable Guest Shell","Run guestshell to open it","Run the Python script",,"The hosting framework and network interface are prepared first, then the container is enabled and used.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.1|topic:meraki|topic:day-0","Place the steps of preparing a new branch with Meraki and the API in the correct order.",,"Create the network","Bind it to the configuration template","Claim the devices into the network","Wait for the devices to come online","Verify the device statuses",,"The network and its template are prepared before devices are claimed. Status checks come after the devices connect.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.1|topic:catalyst-center|topic:pnp","Place the steps of onboarding a device with PnP and Catalyst Center in the correct order.",,"The device contacts the controller and appears as unclaimed","Claim it to a site with an image and a template","The device is provisioned","Check that the state is Provisioned","Verify the device in the inventory",,"A device is claimed after it is discovered, onboarded, and checked in the PnP list and the inventory.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.2|topic:sdwan|topic:python","Place the steps of reading the device list from SD-WAN Manager with Python in the correct order.",,"POST the credentials to /j_security_check","Keep the JSESSIONID cookie","GET /dataservice/client/token","Send GET /dataservice/device with the cookie and the token","Parse the JSON result",,"The session cookie and the token are needed before the inventory call, and the result is parsed last.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.2|topic:catalyst-center|topic:python","Place the steps of a Catalyst Center script that starts work and waits for the result in the correct order.",,"Request a token with basic authentication","Send the request with the X-Auth-Token header","Read the taskId from the response","Poll the task until it finishes","Read the result",,"The call authenticates, starts an asynchronous task, and the script polls the task until it is complete.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|topic:jinja2","Place the steps of developing a Jinja2 template for a branch configuration in the correct order.",,"Write the variable data for one branch","Write the template with loops and conditions","Render it","Compare the output with the expected configuration","Add the data of other branches",,"A template is developed against one example, checked, and then used for more data.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.4|topic:ansible|topic:meraki","Place the steps of running a cisco.meraki playbook in the correct order.",,"Install the cisco.meraki collection","Store the API key in a vault or an environment variable","Write the task with the network name and state present","Run the playbook","Run it again and expect no changes",,"The collection and the secret come first, then the task is written and run, and a second run shows idempotence.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.5|topic:ise|topic:security","Place the steps of quarantining an endpoint with ISE ANC in the correct order.",,"Create the ANC policy","Apply the policy to the endpoint's MAC address","ISE sends a change of authorization","The authorization policy restricts the endpoint","Clear the policy when the endpoint is clean",,"The policy exists before it is applied, the change of authorization makes the network enforce it, and clearing it restores access.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.5|topic:meraki|topic:security","Place the steps of changing the Meraki L3 firewall rules safely through the API in the correct order.",,"GET the current rules","Edit the list in the script","PUT the complete list","Check the response","GET the rules again to confirm",,"The rule list is replaced as a whole, so the current rules are read, edited and sent back in full, and the result is confirmed.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.6|objective:cisco:350-901:1.6|topic:troubleshooting|topic:rest-api","Place the steps of troubleshooting a failing REST call to a controller in the correct order.",,"Read the status code and the body","Check the URL and the HTTP method","Check the authentication and the headers","Repeat the call with curl","Fix the cause and run the script again",,"The response says what went wrong, and the request is checked from the outside in before the fix is applied.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.1|topic:meraki|topic:validation","Place the steps of validating a Meraki change with live tools in the correct order.",,"Apply the change","Start a ping from the device with the live tools API","Poll the result with the returned ID","Read loss and latency","Record the result",,"A live tool request returns an ID, the result is polled, and the numbers are read.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.2|objective:cisco:350-901:2.4|topic:cml|topic:simulation","Place the steps of testing an automation change in CML in the correct order.",,"Import the topology file","Start the lab","Apply the automation","Run the validation tests","Stop and wipe the lab",,"The lab is built and started before the change is applied and tested, and then it is cleaned up.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.3|topic:catalyst-center|topic:swim","Place the steps of upgrading a device with Catalyst Center SWIM in the correct order.",,"Import the image","Mark it as the golden image","Distribute it to the device","Activate it","Check the compliance and the running version",,"An image is imported and chosen, copied to the device and activated, and the result is verified.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.4|topic:thousandeyes","Place the steps of creating a ThousandEyes test with the API in the correct order.",,"Generate a bearer token","List the agents with GET /v7/agents","Choose the agents for the test","Create the test with POST /v7/tests/agent-to-server","Read the results",,"The token and the agents are needed before the test is created, and the results are read after it has run.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.5|objective:cisco:350-901:3.1|topic:telemetry|topic:mdt","Place the steps of configuring an IOS XE telemetry subscription in the correct order.",,"Create the subscription","Set the filter xpath","Choose the stream and the encoding","Set the update policy","Configure the receiver",,"The subscription is built from what to send, how to encode it, how often, and where to send it.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.6|objective:cisco:350-901:3.2|topic:webhooks","Place the steps of reacting to a Catalyst Center event with a webhook in the correct order.",,"Create a REST subscription endpoint with the receiver URL","Subscribe the events to that endpoint","An event occurs","Catalyst Center sends the payload","The receiver verifies it and starts the action",,"The receiver and subscription exist before an event is sent. The receiver checks the message before it acts.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.1|topic:ai|topic:analytics","Place the steps of how an analytics platform flags an anomaly in the correct order.",,"Collect telemetry from the network","Learn the baseline for the site","Compare new data with the baseline","Flag the deviation","Show the issue with the likely cause",,"Data is collected and a baseline is learned. New data is compared with it, and a deviation becomes an issue.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.2|objective:cisco:350-901:4.1|objective:cisco:300-635:5.1|topic:ai|topic:code-validation","Place the steps of safely adopting an AI-written script in the correct order.",,"Write the prompt with the API specification","Read the generated code","Run linting and unit tests","Run it in a lab","Merge through review",,"Context improves the draft, and review and tests come before the lab and the merge.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.3|objective:cisco:350-901:4.2|objective:cisco:300-635:5.2|topic:ai|topic:ai-security","Place the steps of handling a suspected prompt injection in a network agent in the correct order.",,"Detect unexpected tool calls in the logs","Disable the agent's write tools","Review which instructions it followed","Rotate the credentials that it could use","Add input filtering and approval before re-enabling it",,"The agent is contained first, the cause is found, credentials are rotated, and controls are added before it returns.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.4|objective:cisco:350-901:4.3|objective:cisco:300-635:5.3|topic:mcp","Place the steps of publishing a read-only MCP tool in the correct order.",,"Create the FastMCP instance","Write a typed function and decorate it with @mcp.tool","Test it with a client","Add the server to the client configuration","The agent lists and calls the tool",,"The server is built and tested before the client is configured, and the agent then discovers the tool.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.1|objective:cisco:350-901:3.4|objective:cisco:300-635:4.2|topic:pyats|topic:validation","Place the steps of validating a network change with pyATS in the correct order.",,"Describe the devices in the testbed file","Learn the features and save the pre-change snapshot","Apply the change","Learn the features again and save the post-change snapshot","Compare the snapshots with a diff","Review the differences against the expected result","The testbed identifies the devices, the baseline is saved before the change, and the comparison is reviewed afterwards.",3,2

slotfill[30]{tags,text,exhibit,a1,a2,a3,a4,a5,d1,d2,d3,explanation,bloom,difficulty}:
  "objective:cisco:300-435:1.2|objective:cisco:350-901:1.3|topic:restconf","Fill in each blank so that the request creates a new interface entry below the interfaces container with a JSON body.","```bash\ncurl -k -u admin:C1sco123 -X ⟦1⟧ -H 'Content-Type: application/⟦2⟧' https://192.0.2.10/restconf/data/ietf-interfaces:interfaces -d @payload.json\n```","POST","yang-data+json",,,,"GET","DELETE","OPTIONS","POST creates a child resource in the container, and the body uses the yang-data+json media type. GET reads, DELETE removes and OPTIONS asks about the allowed methods.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:1.4|objective:cisco:300-635:1.5|topic:yang|topic:xml","Fill in each blank so that the XML uses the namespace of the module and binds the prefix for the interface type.","```xml\n<interfaces xmlns=\"⟦1⟧\">\n  <interface>\n    <name>Loopback10</name>\n    <type xmlns:ianaift=\"urn:ietf:params:xml:ns:yang:iana-if-type\">⟦2⟧:softwareLoopback</type>\n  </interface>\n</interfaces>\n```","urn:ietf:params:xml:ns:yang:ietf-interfaces","ianaift",,,,"ietf-interfaces","iana-if-type","urn:ietf:params:netconf:base:1.0","The element uses the namespace URI of the module, and the identityref value uses the prefix that is bound to the iana-if-type namespace. A module name is not a namespace, and the base namespace belongs to the protocol.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:1.3|objective:cisco:350-901:2.7|objective:cisco:300-635:1.5|topic:yang|topic:json","Fill in each blank so that the JSON payload follows the YANG encoding rules.","```json\n{\n  \"⟦1⟧:interfaces\": {\n    \"interface\": [\n      {\"name\": \"Loopback10\", \"type\": \"iana-if-type:⟦2⟧\", \"enabled\": ⟦3⟧}\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```","ietf-interfaces","softwareLoopback","true",,,"interfaces","loopback","\"true\"","The top-level member is qualified with the module name, an identityref from another module is prefixed with that module, and a boolean is written without quotes. The other values break these rules.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:1.4|topic:netmiko","Fill in each blank so that the script connects to an IOS XE switch, enters privileged mode, and returns parsed output.","```python\nfrom netmiko import ConnectHandler\n\ndef brief(host):\n    # Purpose: return parsed interface status from one IOS XE switch\n    conn = ConnectHandler(device_type='⟦1⟧', host=host, username='admin', password='C1sco123', secret='C1sco123')\n    conn.⟦2⟧()\n    out = conn.⟦3⟧('show ip interface brief', use_textfsm=True)\n    conn.disconnect()\n    return out\n```","cisco_xe","enable","send_command",,,"cisco_xr","config_mode","send_config_set","cisco_xe is the platform type for IOS XE, enable enters privileged mode, and send_command runs an operational command. cisco_xr is for IOS XR, config_mode enters configuration mode, and send_config_set sends configuration.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.2|objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|objective:cisco:350-901:1.4|topic:ncclient|topic:netconf","Fill in each blank so that ncclient reads the running configuration with a subtree filter over the NETCONF port.","```python\nfrom ncclient import manager\n\ndef read_interfaces(host, flt):\n    # Purpose: read the interface configuration with a subtree filter\n    with manager.connect(host=host, port=⟦1⟧, username='admin', password='C1sco123', hostkey_verify=False) as m:\n        return m.get_config(source='⟦2⟧', filter=('⟦3⟧', flt)).xml\n```","830","running","subtree",,,"443","startup","xpath","NETCONF over SSH uses port 830, the running datastore holds the active configuration, and a subtree filter is selected by the word subtree. Port 443 is HTTPS, startup is the boot configuration, and xpath is another filter type.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.3|objective:cisco:350-901:1.3|topic:restconf|topic:python","Fill in each blank so that the request changes one interface with a PATCH, using the right media type and the encoded key.","```python\nimport requests\n\nurl = f'https://{host}/restconf/data/Cisco-IOS-XE-native:native/interface/GigabitEthernet=⟦3⟧'\nhdr = {'Content-Type': 'application/⟦2⟧'}\nr = requests.⟦1⟧(url, auth=('admin', 'C1sco123'), headers=hdr, json=body, verify=False)\n```","patch","yang-data+json","1%2F0%2F1",,,"put","json","1/0/1","patch merges the body into the resource, the media type is yang-data+json, and the slashes in the list key are percent-encoded. put would replace the resource, and unencoded slashes are read as path separators.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.4|topic:ansible","Fill in each blank so that the lines are applied under the interface section and the configuration is saved only when it differs.","```yaml\n- cisco.ios.ios_config:\n    ⟦1⟧:\n      - ip address 192.0.2.1 255.255.255.0\n    ⟦2⟧: interface GigabitEthernet1\n    ⟦3⟧: modified\n```","lines","parents","save_when",,,"before","after","match","lines holds the commands, parents names the section they belong to, and save_when modified saves the configuration when running and startup differ. before, after and match have other roles.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.5|objective:cisco:350-901:1.4|topic:ztp|topic:day-0","Fill in each blank so that the ZTP script applies the configuration and then saves it.","```python\nfrom cli import ⟦1⟧, ⟦2⟧\n\ndef day0():\n    # Purpose: apply the base configuration and save it\n    ⟦2⟧(['hostname EDGE-01', 'username netops privilege 15 secret S3cr3t!'])\n    ⟦1⟧('write memory')\n\nday0()\n```","cli","configure",,,,"clip","configurep","ztp","configure applies configuration commands, and cli runs an exec command and returns its output. clip and configurep print instead, and ztp is not a function of the cli module.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.6|topic:netconf|topic:troubleshooting","Fill in each blank to check the programmability processes and the NETCONF sessions on IOS XE.","```text\nSwitch# show platform software ⟦1⟧-management process\nSwitch# show ⟦2⟧-yang sessions\n```","yang","netconf",,,,"restconf","ssh","gnmi","The yang-management process listing shows whether the model-driven processes run, and show netconf-yang sessions lists the NETCONF sessions. The other words do not form these commands.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:2.7|topic:eem","Fill in each blank so that the applet reacts to a syslog message, enters privileged mode, and generates a syslog message.","```text\nevent manager applet LINK-DOWN\n event ⟦1⟧ pattern \"changed state to down\"\n action 1.0 cli command \"⟦2⟧\"\n action 2.0 ⟦3⟧ msg \"Interface down detected\"\n```","syslog","enable","syslog",,,"timer","show version","snmp-trap","The syslog detector matches the message, the first CLI action enters privileged mode, and the syslog action writes a message. timer is another detector, and snmp-trap sends a trap instead.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.1|topic:meraki|topic:day-0","Fill in each blank so that the script claims devices into a network and binds the network to a configuration template.","```python\nimport meraki\n\ndef prepare(network_id, serials, template_id):\n    # Purpose: claim devices into a Meraki network and bind a template\n    dashboard = meraki.DashboardAPI(suppress_logging=True)\n    dashboard.networks.⟦1⟧(network_id, serials=serials)\n    dashboard.networks.⟦2⟧(network_id, configTemplateId=template_id)\n```","claimNetworkDevices","bindNetwork",,,,"claimIntoOrganization","createNetwork","updateNetwork","claimNetworkDevices puts devices into a network, and bindNetwork binds the network to a template. claimIntoOrganization claims into the organization inventory, and the others create or change a network.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.1|topic:catalyst-center|topic:pnp","Fill in each blank with the PnP path that adds a device in advance and the path that assigns it to a site.","```text\nPOST /dna/intent/api/v1/onboarding/pnp-device/⟦1⟧\nPOST /dna/intent/api/v1/onboarding/pnp-device/⟦2⟧\n```","import","site-claim",,,,"unclaim","sync","delete","import adds devices to the PnP list ahead of time, and site-claim claims a device to a site. unclaim, sync and delete are other operations.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.2|topic:sdwan|topic:python","Fill in each blank so that the script logs in to SD-WAN Manager and sends the token with later requests.","```python\nr = s.post(f'https://{host}/⟦1⟧', data={'j_username': u, 'j_password': p}, verify=False)\nt = s.get(f'https://{host}/dataservice/client/⟦2⟧', verify=False).text\ns.headers.update({'⟦3⟧': t})\n```","j_security_check","token","X-XSRF-TOKEN",,,"login","session","X-Auth-Token","The login is a form POST to /j_security_check, the token comes from /dataservice/client/token, and it is sent in X-XSRF-TOKEN. X-Auth-Token belongs to Catalyst Center.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.2|objective:cisco:350-901:1.6|topic:meraki|topic:python","Fill in each blank so that the function returns the names of the offline devices of an organization.","```python\nimport meraki\n\ndef offline_devices(org_id):\n    # Purpose: list the names of the offline devices of an organization\n    dashboard = meraki.DashboardAPI(suppress_logging=True)\n    rows = dashboard.organizations.⟦1⟧(org_id, total_pages='all', statuses=['⟦2⟧'])\n    return [r['name'] for r in rows]\n```","getOrganizationDevicesStatuses","offline",,,,"getOrganizationDevices","online","getNetworkDevices","The statuses call returns the status of every device and can be filtered by status. The other calls list devices without their status or work on one network.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|topic:jinja2","Fill in each blank so that no comma follows the last VLAN, the number of VLANs is counted, and a name is printed only if it exists.","```jinja\n{% for vlan in vlans %}\nvlan {{ vlan.id }}{{ \",\" if not loop.⟦1⟧ }}\n{% endfor %}\n{% set total = vlans | ⟦2⟧ %}\n{% if vlan.name ⟦3⟧ defined %}name {{ vlan.name }}{% endif %}\n```","last","length","is",,,"first","count","in","loop.last is true in the final iteration, the length filter counts items, and the is defined test checks that a value exists. loop.first, count and in do not fit these places.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.4|topic:ansible|topic:meraki","Fill in each blank so that the task creates an appliance network if it does not exist.","```yaml\n- cisco.meraki.meraki_network:\n    auth_key: \"{{ vault_key }}\"\n    org_name: Example\n    net_name: Branch-01\n    type: ⟦1⟧\n    state: ⟦2⟧\n```","appliance","present",,,,"switch","absent","query","type names the product family, here an appliance network, and state present creates the network when it is missing. absent deletes it and query only reads.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.5|topic:ise|topic:security","Fill in each blank so that the request applies an ANC policy to an endpoint through the ERS API.","```python\nr = requests.⟦1⟧('https://ise.example.com:⟦2⟧/ers/config/ancendpoint/apply', json=body, auth=(u, p), headers=h, verify=False)\n```","put","9060",,,,"post","443","8910","The ANC apply operation is a PUT to the ERS API, which listens on port 9060. 443 serves the OpenAPI and 8910 is the pxGrid port.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.5|topic:meraki|topic:security","Fill in each blank so that the script reads the L3 firewall rules, adds a rule at the top, and sends the whole list back.","```python\nrules = dashboard.appliance.⟦1⟧(network_id)['rules']\nrules.insert(0, new_rule)\ndashboard.appliance.⟦2⟧(network_id, rules=rules)\n```","getNetworkApplianceFirewallL3FirewallRules","updateNetworkApplianceFirewallL3FirewallRules",,,,"getNetworkApplianceFirewallL7FirewallRules","createNetwork","updateNetworkApplianceVlan","The L3 rule list is read and replaced as a whole with the get and update calls. The L7 call reads other rules, and the others do not handle firewall rules.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:3.6|objective:cisco:350-901:1.6|topic:troubleshooting|topic:rest-api","Fill in each blank so that the script waits when it is rate limited and refreshes the token when it is rejected.","```python\nr = requests.get(url, headers=h, verify=False)\nif r.status_code == ⟦1⟧:\n    time.sleep(int(r.headers['⟦2⟧']))\nelif r.status_code == ⟦3⟧:\n    h['X-Auth-Token'] = new_token()\n```","429","Retry-After","401",,,"403","Location","500","429 means that the rate limit was exceeded and Retry-After gives the wait, while 401 means that the token is missing or expired. 403 means no permission, and 500 is a server error.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.1|topic:meraki|topic:validation","Fill in each blank with the live tool and the identifier that a script uses to read the result of a ping.","```text\nPOST /api/v1/devices/{serial}/liveTools/⟦1⟧\nGET  /api/v1/devices/{serial}/liveTools/ping/⟦2⟧\n```","ping","pingId",,,,"cableTest","throughputTest","macTable","A live tool request starts the ping, and the result is read with the ID that the first call returns. The other names are different live tools.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.2|objective:cisco:350-901:2.4|topic:cml|topic:simulation","Fill in each blank so that the script creates a lab, starts it, and waits until the nodes have converged.","```python\nlab = client.⟦1⟧(title='ci-test')\nr1 = lab.create_node('r1', 'iosv', 0, 0)\nlab.⟦2⟧()\nlab.⟦3⟧()\n```","create_lab","start","wait_until_lab_converged",,,"import_lab","stop","wipe","create_lab makes an empty lab, start boots the nodes, and wait_until_lab_converged blocks until they are ready. import_lab, stop and wipe do not do these things.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.3|topic:catalyst-center|topic:swim","Fill in each blank with the SWIM paths that copy an image to a device and boot the device with it.","```text\nPOST /dna/intent/api/v1/image/⟦1⟧\nPOST /dna/intent/api/v1/image/⟦2⟧/device\n```","distribution","activation",,,,"importation","compliance","golden","Distribution copies the image to the device, and activation boots it. Importation adds an image to the repository, and the other words are different features.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.4|topic:thousandeyes","Fill in each blank so that the requests list the agents and the tests with the current API version.","```python\nh = {'Authorization': 'Bearer ' + token}\nagents = requests.get('https://api.thousandeyes.com/⟦1⟧/agents', headers=h).json()\ntests = requests.get('https://api.thousandeyes.com/v7/⟦2⟧', headers=h).json()\n```","v7","tests",,,,"v6","alerts","api","The documented base URI is api.thousandeyes.com/v7, and the tests resource lists configured tests. v6 is an older version, alerts lists alerts, and api is not a path segment.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.5|objective:cisco:350-901:3.1|topic:telemetry|topic:mdt","Fill in each blank to complete the configured subscription.","```text\ntelemetry ietf subscription 101\n encoding encode-kvgpb\n filter xpath /process-cpu-ios-xe-oper:cpu-usage/cpu-utilization/five-seconds\n stream ⟦1⟧\n update-policy ⟦2⟧ 1000\n receiver ip address 192.0.2.50 57500 protocol ⟦3⟧\n```","yang-push","periodic","grpc-tcp",,,"yang-notif-native","on-change","tls-native","The yang-push stream carries data on a schedule, the periodic policy takes an interval in centiseconds, and grpc-tcp is the dial-out transport. on-change takes no interval.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.6|topic:meraki|topic:webhooks","Fill in each blank so that the receiver checks the shared secret of the Meraki webhook and starts the action for the alert type.","```python\n@app.post('/meraki')\ndef hook():\n    # Purpose: accept a Meraki webhook only when the shared secret matches\n    body = request.get_json()\n    if body.get('⟦1⟧') != SECRET:\n        return '', 401\n    start_action(body['⟦2⟧'])\n    return '', 200\n```","sharedSecret","alertType",,,,"secret","type","event","The Meraki payload carries the shared secret in sharedSecret and names the kind of alert in alertType. The other keys are not in the payload.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:4.4|topic:catalyst-center|topic:monitoring","Fill in each blank with the Catalyst Center resources for the health of the network devices and of the clients.","```python\nnet = requests.get(f'{base}/dna/intent/api/v1/⟦1⟧', headers=h).json()\ncli = requests.get(f'{base}/dna/intent/api/v1/⟦2⟧', headers=h).json()\n```","network-health","client-health",,,,"topology","issues","task","network-health reports the health of the network devices and client-health that of the clients. topology, issues and task are other resources.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.1|topic:ai|topic:analytics","Fill in each blank so that the function flags a value that is more than three standard deviations away from the learned baseline.","```python\ndef is_anomaly(value, mean, std):\n    # Purpose: flag a value that deviates strongly from the learned baseline\n    return abs(value - ⟦1⟧) > ⟦2⟧ * std\n```","mean","3",,,,"median","0","value","A value is compared with the baseline mean, and the limit is a multiple of the standard deviation. The median is another measure, and a limit of zero would flag everything.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.2|objective:cisco:350-901:4.1|objective:cisco:300-635:5.1|topic:ai|topic:code-validation","Fill in each blank so that the unit test checks AI-generated code without calling a real controller.","```python\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\n\ndef test_get_devices():\n    # Purpose: check that the generated function parses the controller reply\n    with patch('requests.⟦1⟧') as get:\n        get.return_value.json.return_value = {'response': [{'hostname': 'sw1'}]}\n        assert get_devices() == ['⟦2⟧']\n```","get","sw1",,,,"post","sw2","put","The function under test calls requests.get, so that is the call to replace, and the expected result is the hostname in the fake reply. post and put are not used, and sw2 is not in the data.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.3|objective:cisco:350-901:4.2|objective:cisco:300-635:5.2|topic:ai|topic:ai-security","Fill in each blank so that the agent can run only the tools that were approved for it.","```python\nALLOWED_TOOLS = {'get_status', 'list_interfaces'}\n\ndef run_tool(name, args):\n    # Purpose: run only the tools that were approved for the agent\n    if name not in ⟦1⟧:\n        raise PermissionError(name)\n    return TOOLS[name](**⟦2⟧)\n```","ALLOWED_TOOLS","args",,,,"TOOLS","name","tool","The check compares the requested name with the approved set, and the approved arguments are passed to the function. Checking against TOOLS would allow every registered tool.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-435:5.4|objective:cisco:350-901:4.3|objective:cisco:300-635:5.3|topic:mcp","Fill in each blank so that the first function is exposed as read-only data at a URI and the second as a reusable prompt.","```python\n@mcp.⟦1⟧('devices://{site}/inventory')\ndef inventory(site: str) -> str:\n    # Purpose: return the device inventory of a site as read-only context\n    return load_inventory(site)\n\n@mcp.⟦2⟧()\ndef triage(device: str) -> str:\n    # Purpose: return a prompt that guides the triage of a device\n    return f'Triage the device {device}'\n```","resource","prompt",,,,"tool","run","server","The resource decorator exposes data at a URI, and the prompt decorator exposes a reusable prompt template. tool exposes an action, and run and server are not decorators.",2,2
